{"abstract":[{"text":"The lexicographically first largest clique: of all the largest cliques, the least by vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index, in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ignored. Of two cliques of one size, the lesser is the one holding the least vertex of their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symmetric difference. After ","type":"text"},{"code":"cliqueNumber()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s search, each largest clique is searched for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from its first vertex v in degeneracy order, among v’s later neighbors, so memory stays O(n +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"m + degeneracy²) however large a hub’s degree. For each v, a witness clique W (any one of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the right size) guides a pass over the candidates in ascending number: a candidate in W is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"taken, any other is taken exactly when a search finds the rest of a clique among the common","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"neighbors left (which then becomes W). A v whose candidates all exceed the least vertex of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the best clique so far is skipped. Up to one search per vertex and candidate, each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exponential in the worst case, so it can be far slower than ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximumClique()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; the search","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"does not check for task cancellation.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexi